# M&E isolation (cardinal rule)

## One-way dependency

- **`app/reports/` may import core** (`app.services`, `app.models`, `app.core`, `app.ai`, `app.integrations`, `app.api.dependencies`).
- **Core must NEVER import `app.reports`.** Enforced by `.cursor/hooks/isolation_veto.py`.

## Single mounting seam (backend)

The **only** core file that may reference M&E is `app/main.py`, and only as:

```python
if settings.ME_MODULE_ENABLED:
    from app.reports.router import router as reports_router
    app.include_router(reports_router)
```

No other `app.reports` imports anywhere under core paths.

## Single mounting seam (frontend — separate repo)

- Feature flag (e.g. `NEXT_PUBLIC_ME_MODULE_ENABLED`) + `/reports/*` routes.
- Un-mount API router + flag off UI = code kill switch.

## Data isolation

- Four M&E tables only; FKs **inward** to core (`users`, `proposals` nullable).
- **No** core table FKs to M&E tables.
- **No** core migration alters core tables for M&E.

## Runtime isolation

- Agent pipeline runs in **background worker** (`Procfile` worker line), not sync API path.
- Worker scale-to-0 = runtime kill switch.

See `docs/artefacts/me_module/ME_MODULE_KILL_SWITCH.md` and `REPO_MAP_ME_MODULE.md`.
